  "authoringNotes": {
    "status": "approximate corridor: OpenStreetMap road axes (dual carriageways averaged) checked against the GSI 1979–1983 (gazo2) and 1974–1978 (gazo1) aerial layers; the 1984–1986 (gazo3) and 1988–1990 (gazo4) layers return HTTP 404 for central Kyoto. Not surveyed or native-qualified.",
    "closedCircuit": "Kyoto Station front on Shiokoji-dori → Kyoto Tower corner → Karasuma-dori past Higashi Honganji → Shijo-dori east over Shijo Ohashi and the Keihan level crossing, past Minamiza and Gion → Yasaka west gate T → Higashioji-dori north → Sanjo-dori east beside the Keishin street tramway → Keage hairpin → south end of Shirakawa-dori past the brick power station and the incline → Niomon-dori west along the canal → Jingu-michi north under the great torii → Nijo-dori west → Higashioji-dori north → Marutamachi-dori west over the Kamo and past the Gyoen → Horikawa-dori south past Nijo Castle and Nishi Honganji → Shiokoji-dori east to the station.",
    "lapsReason": "One 13.18 km lap shows the whole tour once without repeating streets. The repository's own single-car handling graph and practice AI (pace.ts) take 3:24.7–3:28.9 here and 3:46–4:25 on Tokyo; scaled by the recorded eight-car Tokyo race (6,841–8,462 ticks) the eight-car field should finish in about 3:26–4:15, inside the 5:00 cap. targetMs is the 3:27 good-driver estimate, not a measured human drive.",
    "elevationsAndWidths": "Elevations: GSI DEM5A tiles every 10 m along the axis, ±40 m smoothing, Shijo Ohashi and Marutamachi-bashi spans interpolated, Keage hairpin hand-set. Widths: Shijo 15 m carriageway before the 2015 narrowing (sourced); Karasuma 20.3 m kerb to kerb from the 2018 MLIT cross-section (1986 assumed similar, unconfirmed); the rest estimated from the aerials and modern lane counts. Not historical survey measurements.",
    "directions": "Every street is driven in a direction that is legal today. Karasuma, Shijo, Higashioji, Sanjo, Marutamachi, Horikawa and Shiokoji were two-way arterials in 1986; the 1986 regulation of the Keage connector, Niomon-dori east of Higashioji, Jingu-michi and Okazaki Nijo-dori, and the legality of the Sanjo-to-connector left turn at Keage in 1986, are unconfirmed.",
    "rail": "Crosses the at-grade Keihan main line at the east end of Shijo Ohashi (Shijo crossing barriers from November 1982; line underground from 24 May 1987). Shares Sanjo-dori with the Keishin line's street track from Higashiyama-Sanjo to the Keage stop (closed after 11 October 1997). Kyoto City Trams were abolished on 30 September 1978; no tram tracks on Shijo, Higashioji, Marutamachi, Karasuma or Horikawa.",
    "musicCues": "Placeholder asset and hash. Cues mark the start at the 1952 station, Shijo Ohashi and Gion, the Sanjo tramway climb to Keage, the Okazaki torii, the Kamo crossing at Marutamachi, and the Nijo Castle–Horikawa home run, from single-car gate splits scaled to targetMs.",
    "notForProfile": "Current RaceV1 accepts only 3 tracks/5400 ticks. This input cannot be submitted to it.",
    "cornerGeometry": "Quadratic tangent trims in millimetres, not physical circular radii. The start gate is on the straight in front of the station (zero trim), about 120 m before the Kyoto Tower corner. The Keage hairpin is a ten-vertex, 24 m-radius polygon with a 9 m half-width standing for the open Y-junction; the 1986 kerb layout there is unconfirmed. Okazaki's narrow corners use 24–30 m trims so the practice AI does not pin itself against the inside wall."
  },
